# Core Development Rules

> Martial-arts style: short, direct, no fluff. Every token counts.

---

## Agent Behavior

- Read existing code BEFORE writing anything. Understand patterns first.
- Project rules: `clean-code.mdc` + `react-state-performance.mdc` (always-on). Community rules/skills: `.cursor/COMMUNITY-MANIFEST.md`.
- Never assume. If context is missing, ask ONE clarifying question.
- Don't apologize for errors — fix them.
- If code is incomplete, add `// TODO:` comments instead of leaving it broken.
- After generating code, mentally check: "Does this match existing patterns in the codebase?"
- Keep SOLID but simple — separation of concerns without over-engineering.

---

## Size Limits

| Unit | Limit | Action if exceeded |
|------|-------|--------------------|
| File | 300 lines | Split into modules |
| Function | 30–50 lines | Extract sub-functions |
| Parameters | 3–4 max | Use object/options pattern |
| Rule file | 500 lines | Split into scoped `.mdc` files |

