## UI/UX — Shadcn + Accessibility (Required)

- **Use Shadcn components** for common UI primitives (Button, Input, Select, Dropdown, Tooltip, Dialog, Toast).
  - Avoid raw `<button>`/`<input>`/`<select>` unless there is a clear reason.
- **Accessibility is not optional**:
  - Every interactive element must have an accessible name (`aria-label` or visible label).
  - Preserve keyboard navigation (Tab order, Enter/Space to activate).
  - Use `role="toolbar"` + `role="group"` only when semantics are correct.
- **Feedback states**:
  - Always handle: empty state, loading, error.
  - Disable buttons when action is not applicable; provide tooltip if unclear.
- **Forms / inputs**:
  - Number inputs: set `min/max/step`, clamp/validate on change.
  - Debounce high-frequency updates if they cause jank (canvas edits, sliders).
- **Visual consistency**:
  - Use design tokens/util classes consistently (spacing, borders, colors).
  - Keep clickable targets >= 32px and maintain clear hover/focus styles.

