## Backend Architecture — Service Layer Required

Every endpoint's business logic lives in a **service**, never in the controller/handler.

```
src/
  controllers/    ← HTTP layer: parse request, call service, return response
  services/       ← Business logic, validation, orchestration
  repositories/   ← Database queries only
  models/         ← Data schemas / entities
  middlewares/    ← Auth, logging, error handling
```

```typescript
// ✅ Controller — thin
async function updateUser(req: Request, res: Response) {
  const user = await userService.update(req.params.id, req.body);
  res.json(user);
}

// ✅ Service — all the logic lives here
async function update(id: string, payload: UpdateUserDto) {
  const existing = await userRepository.findById(id);
  if (!existing) throw new NotFoundError('User not found');

  const validated = validateUpdatePayload(payload);
  return userRepository.update(id, validated);
}
```

